# =================================================================
# ABox Instances extracted from:
#   Government Resolution No. 945
#   Complete restatement of Government Resolution No. 818
#   (Cybersecurity Law Implementation) – NIS2 transposition,
#   new incident management plan, subject identification
#   methodology, cybersecurity requirements, enforcement
#   procedures, Secure Network users, payment framework
#   2024-11-06, Vilnius
#   Prime Minister Ingrida Šimonytė
# =================================================================

lld:GovRes-945-2024 a llo:Statute ;
    rdfs:label "Government Resolution No. 945 – Complete restatement of Resolution No. 818 for NIS2 implementation (2024)" ;
    rdfs:label "Government Resolution No. 945 – Complete restatement of Resolution No. 818 for NIS2 implementation (2024)"@en ;
    rdfs:label "Vyriausybės nutarimas Nr. 945 – Nutarimo Nr. 818 išdėstymas nauja redakcija dėl TIS2 įgyvendinimo (2024)"@lt ;
    rdfs:comment "Complete restatement of Government Resolution No. 818 of 2018-08-13 implementing the Cybersecurity Law, aligned with NIS2 Directive (EU) 2022/2555. References Cybersecurity Law Arts. 7(2)(3), 11(6), 14(1)(1) and (2), 28(6), 30(1), 37(1), (2)(3), (4), (6), (8) and (9). Approves six components: (1) National Cyber Incident Management Plan (Nacionalinis kibernetinių incidentų valdymo planas) – defines incident management at subject and national level, Security Operations Centre separation of duties, significant incident criteria (territory-wide disruption, 2+ hour disruption, 1000+ affected users or 25%, financial loss ≥€500K or 10%+ revenue, data breach 10K+ persons, essential function disruption, state/military system impact, multiple subjects/sectors, cross-border impact), 24h-72h-1month reporting timelines, NKVC escalation for extraordinary events; (2) Cybersecurity Subject Identification by Special Criteria Methodology; (3) Cybersecurity Requirements Description – comprehensive organisational and technical requirements with 12 sections covering risk management, access control, multi-factor authentication, cryptography, mobile devices, backup, supplier security, procurement, vulnerability management, incident response, business continuity, and technical controls; (4) Enforcement Measures Application Procedure Description – compliance checks, warnings, fines; (5) Secure State Data Transmission Network users list (hundreds of institutions); (6) Payment criteria and calculation procedure for Secure Network additional services. Also authorises Defence Minister to approve Secure Network service conditions and connection/disconnection procedures. Tasks cybersecurity subjects to automate incident registration in KSIS National Cyber Incident Management Platform within 12 months of registration (extendable once by 12 months). Repeals GovRes 716/2013 (General Electronic Information Security Requirements) and GovRes 27/2018 (Secure Network implementation) with all amendments. PM Ingrida Šimonytė, Defence Minister Laurynas Kasčiūnas." ;
    rdfs:comment "Complete restatement of Government Resolution No. 818 of 2018-08-13 implementing the Cybersecurity Law, aligned with NIS2 Directive (EU) 2022/2555. References Cybersecurity Law Arts. 7(2)(3), 11(6), 14(1)(1) and (2), 28(6), 30(1), 37(1), (2)(3), (4), (6), (8) and (9). Approves six components: (1) National Cyber Incident Management Plan (Nacionalinis kibernetinių incidentų valdymo planas) – defines incident management at subject and national level, Security Operations Centre separation of duties, significant incident criteria (territory-wide disruption, 2+ hour disruption, 1000+ affected users or 25%, financial loss ≥€500K or 10%+ revenue, data breach 10K+ persons, essential function disruption, state/military system impact, multiple subjects/sectors, cross-border impact), 24h-72h-1month reporting timelines, NKVC escalation for extraordinary events; (2) Cybersecurity Subject Identification by Special Criteria Methodology; (3) Cybersecurity Requirements Description – comprehensive organisational and technical requirements with 12 sections covering risk management, access control, multi-factor authentication, cryptography, mobile devices, backup, supplier security, procurement, vulnerability management, incident response, business continuity, and technical controls; (4) Enforcement Measures Application Procedure Description – compliance checks, warnings, fines; (5) Secure State Data Transmission Network users list (hundreds of institutions); (6) Payment criteria and calculation procedure for Secure Network additional services. Also authorises Defence Minister to approve Secure Network service conditions and connection/disconnection procedures. Tasks cybersecurity subjects to automate incident registration in KSIS National Cyber Incident Management Platform within 12 months of registration (extendable once by 12 months). Repeals GovRes 716/2013 (General Electronic Information Security Requirements) and GovRes 27/2018 (Secure Network implementation) with all amendments. PM Ingrida Šimonytė, Defence Minister Laurynas Kasčiūnas."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Vyriausybės 2018-08-13 nutarimo Nr. 818 dėl Kibernetinio saugumo įstatymo įgyvendinimo išdėstymas nauja redakcija, suderintas su TIS2 direktyva (ES) 2022/2555. Tvirtina šešis komponentus: (1) Nacionalinį kibernetinių incidentų valdymo planą – incidentų valdymas subjekto ir nacionaliniu lygmeniu, didelio kibernetinio incidento kriterijai, pranešimų terminai 24 val.–72 val.–1 mėn.; (2) Kibernetinio saugumo subjektų identifikavimo pagal specialiuosius kriterijus metodiką; (3) Kibernetinio saugumo reikalavimų aprašą – organizaciniai ir techniniai reikalavimai su 12 skirsnių; (4) Vykdymo užtikrinimo priemonių taikymo tvarkos aprašą; (5) Saugiojo valstybinio duomenų perdavimo tinklo naudotojų sąrašą; (6) Atlyginimo už Saugiojo tinklo papildomas paslaugas tvarkos aprašą. Paveda kibernetinio saugumo subjektams per 12 mėnesių automatizuoti incidentų registravimą KSIS. Pripažįsta netekusiais galios nutarimus Nr. 716/2013 ir Nr. 27/2018. Ministrė Pirmininkė Ingrida Šimonytė, krašto apsaugos ministras Laurynas Kasčiūnas."@lt ;
    llo:hasDocID "No. 945" ;
    llo:dateEnacted "2024-11-06"^^xsd:date ;
    llo:isPubliclyDisclosed true ;
    llo:hasComponent lld:GovRes-945-2024_Point1 ,
                     lld:GovRes-945-2024_Point2 .

