lld:Concept_NIS2ImplementingFramework a llo:LegalConcept ;
    rdfs:label "NIS2 implementing framework under restated Resolution No. 818" ;
    rdfs:label "NIS2 implementing framework under restated Resolution No. 818"@en ;
    rdfs:label "TIS2 įgyvendinimo sistema pagal naują nutarimo Nr. 818 redakciją"@lt ;
    rdfs:comment "Six-component implementing framework for the NIS2-restated Cybersecurity Law: (1) National Cyber Incident Management Plan with SOC requirements and escalation procedures; (2) Subject identification methodology using special criteria for entities not automatically covered by annexes; (3) Comprehensive cybersecurity requirements description with 12 thematic sections; (4) Enforcement measures application procedure; (5) Secure State Data Transmission Network users list; (6) Payment framework for Secure Network services. Mandatory automated incident registration in KSIS National Platform within 12 months of subject registration." ;
    rdfs:comment "Six-component implementing framework for the NIS2-restated Cybersecurity Law: (1) National Cyber Incident Management Plan with SOC requirements and escalation procedures; (2) Subject identification methodology using special criteria for entities not automatically covered by annexes; (3) Comprehensive cybersecurity requirements description with 12 thematic sections; (4) Enforcement measures application procedure; (5) Secure State Data Transmission Network users list; (6) Payment framework for Secure Network services. Mandatory automated incident registration in KSIS National Platform within 12 months of subject registration."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Šešių komponentų TIS2 redakcijos Kibernetinio saugumo įstatymo įgyvendinimo sistema: (1) Nacionalinis kibernetinių incidentų valdymo planas su SOC reikalavimais; (2) Subjektų identifikavimo pagal specialiuosius kriterijus metodika; (3) Kibernetinio saugumo reikalavimų aprašas su 12 teminių skirsnių; (4) Vykdymo užtikrinimo priemonių tvarkos aprašas; (5) Saugiojo tinklo naudotojų sąrašas; (6) Saugiojo tinklo paslaugų apmokėjimo tvarka."@lt ;
    llo:hasLegalBasis "Point 1, GovRes 945/2024 (restated Resolution 818)" .

lld:Concept_SignificantIncidentCriteria a llo:LegalConcept ;
    rdfs:label "Significant cyber incident criteria (NIS2 Art. 18(2) implementation)" ;
    rdfs:label "Significant cyber incident criteria (NIS2 Art. 18(2) implementation)"@en ;
    rdfs:label "Didelio kibernetinio incidento kriterijai (TIS2 18 str. 2 d. įgyvendinimas)"@lt ;
    rdfs:comment "A cyber incident is deemed significant when the subject experiences or may experience major service disruption meeting at least one criterion: (1) territory-wide disruption across Lithuania and/or at least one EU/NATO country; (2) network/system disruption for 2+ hours; (3) 1,000+ affected service recipients or workstations, or 25% (whichever is less); (4) financial loss ≥€500,000 or ≥10% of annual revenue; (5) personal data breach affecting 10,000+ persons; (6) disruption of essential functions; (7) impact on state or military systems; (8) impact on multiple subjects or sectors; (9) cross-border impact. Reporting timeline: 24h early warning, 72h incident notification, 1-month final report." ;
    rdfs:comment "A cyber incident is deemed significant when the subject experiences or may experience major service disruption meeting at least one criterion: (1) territory-wide disruption across Lithuania and/or at least one EU/NATO country; (2) network/system disruption for 2+ hours; (3) 1,000+ affected service recipients or workstations, or 25% (whichever is less); (4) financial loss ≥€500,000 or ≥10% of annual revenue; (5) personal data breach affecting 10,000+ persons; (6) disruption of essential functions; (7) impact on state or military systems; (8) impact on multiple subjects or sectors; (9) cross-border impact. Reporting timeline: 24h early warning, 72h incident notification, 1-month final report."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Kibernetinis incidentas laikomas dideliu, kai subjektas patiria ar gali patirti didelių paslaugų teikimo sutrikimų ir atitinka bent vieną kriterijų: (1) trikdymas visoje LT teritorijoje ir/arba bent vienoje ES/NATO šalyje; (2) 2+ val. trikdymas; (3) 1000+ paveiktų gavėjų arba 25%; (4) ≥500 000 EUR nuostoliai arba ≥10% pajamų; (5) 10 000+ asmenų duomenų pažeidimas; (6) esminių funkcijų sutrikimas; (7) valstybės ar karinių sistemų poveikis; (8) kelių subjektų/sektorių poveikis; (9) tarpvalstybinis poveikis."@lt ;
    llo:hasLegalBasis "Point 9, National Cyber Incident Management Plan (GovRes 945/2024)" .

lld:Concept_EnforcementProcedures a llo:LegalConcept ;
    rdfs:label "Cybersecurity enforcement measures application procedure" ;
    rdfs:label "Cybersecurity enforcement measures application procedure"@en ;
    rdfs:label "Kibernetinio saugumo vykdymo užtikrinimo priemonių taikymo tvarka"@lt ;
    rdfs:comment "New enforcement measures application procedure approved as component 1.4 of restated Resolution 818: establishes the detailed process for NKSC compliance checks, issuance of warnings, and application of fines to cybersecurity subjects for non-compliance with Cybersecurity Law requirements." ;
    rdfs:comment "New enforcement measures application procedure approved as component 1.4 of restated Resolution 818: establishes the detailed process for NKSC compliance checks, issuance of warnings, and application of fines to cybersecurity subjects for non-compliance with Cybersecurity Law requirements."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Naujas vykdymo užtikrinimo priemonių taikymo tvarkos aprašas, patvirtintas kaip nutarimo Nr. 818 naujos redakcijos 1.4 komponentas: nustato detalią NKSC atitikties patikrinimų, įspėjimų ir baudų kibernetinio saugumo subjektams procesą."@lt ;
    llo:hasLegalBasis "Component 1.4, GovRes 945/2024 (restated Resolution 818)" .

